SUMMARY:20s&30s Hike at Mt Watatic
LOCATION:Ashburnham\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 30\, 2025\nhttps://activities.outdoors.org/s
 /oc-activity/a5UUN000001vqpP2AQ/\nLet’s bid a fond farewell to fall with
  one final hike! Climb to the summit of Mt. Wataticwith us to take in spec
 tacular views from its open peak that stretch from Mount Greylockin the we
 st to Boston in the east. Ascend on old cart roads through stands of red m
 apleand white wood asters and then descend back down the rocky western slo
 pe to see..abig rock!This 2.8 mile loop with 700’ of elevation gain is e
 xpected to take 2-3 hours. It’s a veryapproachable trip for novice hiker
 s with good mobility and those who identify asphysically active. We’ll p
 lan to keep a moderate pace (1.5mph) to ensure we staytogether as a group.
  This is a popular hike\, so you can expect a well-trodden dirt pathon the
  ascent. The descent from Mount Watatic is rocky and uneven\, so you mayap
 preciate bringing a set of hiking poles.Daytime highs in Ashburnham and As
 hby have been ranging from just below freezing(32F) to 50F lately\, so mak
 e sure you come dressed in layers and prepared for coldweather. Puffy jack
 ets or a similar insulating layer are a must\, as well as a hat and set of
 gloves/mittens. Mount Watatic’s peak is exposed\, so pack a wind-proof o
 uter layer toward off the chill. Trip leaders will be monitoring the weath
 er for icy conditions inadvance since light rain and freeze/thaw condition
 s are expected in the next coupleweeks.You can expect an email with furthe
 r details\, including the exact meeting time\, one weekin advance of the t
 rip.Any cancellations due to weather will be sent out via email the day be
 fore the trip.Rain\, stormy weather\, or icy conditions will cancel this t
 rip.
END:VEVENT
